meta {
  name: Get the other product this connection’s site offers
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/automation-connections/:automationConnection_id/other-product
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  automationConnection_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  For a connection whose account reaches more than one product (an Atlassian site with Jira and Confluence), what to offer next, seen from the tile it was connected from (`from`: `jira` or `confluence`). `offer.kind` is `grant` (allow the other product with one more sign-in on the same connection, named in `grant`), `turn_on` (turn on the switch named in `switch`, `incident_tickets`) or `ready` (the connection already reaches it), with the product, the `site`, and the current default place (`default_target`, `default_target_name`). `offer` is null when the site does not have the other product, or the offer was dismissed for this connection. Read from what InfraNest recorded; nothing is asked of the tool.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
